"Material agreement entered","kind":"deal","tone":"good"},{"label":"Other material event","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1751008/000175100825000061/0001751008-25-000061-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-06-09","form":"8-K","codes":["5.07"],"events":[{"label":"Shareholder vote results","kind":"governance","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1751008/000175100825000057/0001751008-25-000057-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-05-07","form":"8-K","codes":["1.01","2.02","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Material agreement entered","kind":"deal","tone":"good"},{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1751008/000175100825000051/0001751008-25-000051-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-04-09","form":"8-K","codes":["5.02"],"events":[{"label":"Director or officer departure or appointment","kind":"people","tone":"warn"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1751008/000175100825000032/0001751008-25-000032-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[],"summary":{"sentences":["AppLovin Corp files with the SEC under \"Services-Computer Programming, Data Processing, Etc.\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 4 years.","It reported $5.7bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 59.0% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 88.9%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($2.8bn of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 59.0% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $1.8bn in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1751008/000175100826000044/0001751008-26-000044-index.htm","accession":"0001751008-26-000044"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 6 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1751008/000175100826000044/0001751008-26-000044-index.htm","accession":"0001751008-26-000044"},{"text":"Gross margin of 88.9% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001751008"},{"text":"Gross margin expanded from 86.9% to 88.9% against the same quarter a year earlier - the company is keeping more of what it sells, not buying growth with discounts.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001751008"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $2.8bn over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1751008/000175100826000044/0001751008-26-000044-index.htm","accession":"0001751008-26-000044"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-1.8% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1751008/000175100826000044/0001751008-26-000044-index.htm","accession":"0001751008-26-000044"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 30.7% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1751008/000175100826000044/0001751008-26-000044-index.htm","accession":"0001751008-26-000044"},{"text":"Debt of $3.5bn against equity of $2.4bn. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1751008/000175100826000044/0001751008-26-000044-index.htm","accession":"0001751008-26-000044"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 3.0% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (294,228 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1751008/000120918926000009/0001209189-26-000009-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 81.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.81,"consecutive":2,"current":0.889,"current_display":"88.9%","threshold_display":"81.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 29.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.29,"consecutive":2,"current":0.59,"current_display":"59.0%","threshold_display":"29.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.1,"consecutive":1,"current":-0.018,"current_display":"-1.8%","threshold_display":"10.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 2.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":2.0,"consecutive":1,"current":1.487,"current_display":"1.49","threshold_display":"2.00","fired":false,"rationale":"Past